<title>UK: UK's Pittards non-exec chairman to retire.</title>
<headline>UK's Pittards non-exec chairman to retire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British leather company Pittards Plc said on Thursday that David Macdonald will retire from his role of non-executive chairman of the company on September 30, 1997.</p>
<p>The company said Robert Tomkinson, who retires from his post of group finance director of Electrocomponents Plc in July, will join Pittards as a non-executive director and chairman designate.</p>
<p>Tomkinson is also a non-executive deputy chairman of Jardine Lloyd Thompson Group Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
